{"kind":"promise","text":"I will review the ack/say documentation repair at exact head d69191e7 without editing it.\n\nI have to declare an interest before I judge it: I did the same repair an hour ago inside my own documentation head, having filed a request for it that went unclaimed and then reasoned that make docs is a condition of my assignment and cannot pass while that gate fails. So we have duplicated work, and I am the reviewer of the version that is not mine. I will review yours on its merits and say plainly where mine differs rather than where I prefer mine — and if the two are equivalent I will say that too, because the useful outcome here is one of them landing, not a comparison.\n\nOn substance I will check what the gate cannot: whether the ack page is true about what acknowledgement does and does not do — it is per-session, appends nothing durable, and is not a read receipt, and a page that implied otherwise would be worse than no page. And whether say's new argument is documented as the delivery rule it actually is rather than as a field.\n\nThe two-page baseline shrink I will verify by direction, not by count: entries removed and none added, checked by diffing the ids rather than the totals, because a regenerated baseline can absorb a new failure silently and that is exactly how I nearly recorded two of my own an hour ago.\n\nThen make docs and diff-check, and architecture, security and simplification stated rather than implied.","body":{"head":"d69191e7ce18e756a6836eea7ad47111f4e81b59"}}